I walk out into the stairwell again.
My biggest suitcase stands on the floor.
It is very heavy.
I pull on the suitcase.
Suddenly I hear footsteps on the stairs.
It is my Danish neighbor, Nina.
She smiles warmly at me.
"Are you moving in today, Maya?" she asks.
"Yes, I am finally in my new apartment," I say.
"I will help you," Nina says kindly.
She grabs hold of the suitcase.
Together we carry the suitcase into the living room.
Nina sets it carefully on the floor.
Now the suitcase stands by the large window.
There already lies a bag under the window.
"Thank you very much for the help, Nina," I say happily.
"You are welcome," she smiles.
I am very happy with my new apartment and my sweet neighbor.
